			part=strings.TrimSpace(part[1:])
			if part=="" { return nil, fmt.Errorf("empty has after combinator") }
		}
		cx, err:=cssParseComplex(part)
		if err!=nil { return nil, err }
		out=append(out,&cssRelative{combinator: comb, sel: cx})
	}
	return out, nil
}

// ---------- matching ----------

func cssElementParent(n *domNode) *domNode {
	if n==nil || n.Parent==nil { return nil }
	if n.Parent.Type==nodeElement { return n.Parent }
	return nil
}
func cssElementSiblings(n *domNode) []*domNode {
	if n.Parent==nil { return []*domNode{n} }
	var out []*domNode
	for _,c:=range n.Parent.Children {
		if c.Type==nodeElement { out=append(out,c) }
	}
	return out
}
func cssPrevElementSibling(n *domNode) *domNode {
	sibs:=cssElementSiblings(n)
	for i, s:=range sibs { if s==n && i>0 { return sibs[i-1] } }
	return nil
}
func cssNextElementSibling(n *domNode) *domNode {
	sibs:=cssElementSiblings(n)
	for i,s:=range sibs { if s==n && i+1<len(sibs) { return sibs[i+1] } }
	return nil
}

func cssMatchesComplex(n *domNode, cx *cssComplex) bool {
	return cssMatchPart(n, cx, len(cx.parts)-1)
}
func cssMatchPart(n *domNode, cx *cssComplex, idx int) bool {
	if n==nil || n.Type!=nodeElement { return false }
	if !cssMatchesCompound(n, cx.parts[idx].compound) { return false }
	if idx==0 { return true }
	comb:=cx.parts[idx].combinator
	switch comb {
	case '>':
		return cssMatchPart(cssElementParent(n), cx, idx-1)
	case ' ':
		for p:=cssElementParent(n); p!=nil; p=cssElementParent(p) {
			if cssMatchPart(p,cx,idx-1) { return true }
		}
		return false
	case '+':
		return cssMatchPart(cssPrevElementSibling(n), cx, idx-1)
	case '~':
		for s:=cssPrevElementSibling(n); s!=nil; s=cssPrevElementSibling(s) {
			if cssMatchPart(s,cx,idx-1) { return true }
		}
		return false
	}
	return false
}

func cssMatchesCompound(n *domNode, comp *cssCompound) bool {
	if comp.tag!="" && comp.tag!="*" {
		if !strings.EqualFold(n.Local, comp.tag) { return false }
	}
	if comp.hasID {
		v,ok:=n.getAttrExact("id")
		if !ok || v!=comp.id { return false }
	}
	for _,cond:=range comp.conds {
		if !cssMatchesCond(n, cond) { return false }
	}
	return true
}

func cssMatchesCond(n *domNode, cond cssCond) bool {
	switch cond.kind {
	case "class":
		v,ok:=n.getAttrExact("class")
		if !ok { return false }
		for _,f:=range strings.Fields(v) { if f==cond.class { return true } }
		return false
	case "attr":
		v,ok:=n.getAttrExact(cond.attrName)
		if cond.attrOp=="" { return ok }
		if !ok {
			// != with missing attr: cascadia treats as ??? check: value not equal
			if cond.attrOp=="!=" { return true }
			return false
		}
		val:=cond.attrVal
		actual:=v
		if cond.attrFlag=="i" { actual=strings.ToLower(actual); val=strings.ToLower(val) }
		switch cond.attrOp {
		case "=": return actual==val
		case "!=": return actual!=val
		case "~=":
			if val=="" { return false }
			for _,f:=range strings.Fields(actual) { if f==val { return true } }
			return false
		case "|=": return actual==val || strings.HasPrefix(actual, val+"-")
		case "^=": if val=="" { return false }; return strings.HasPrefix(actual,val)
		case "$=": if val=="" { return false }; return strings.HasSuffix(actual,val)
		case "*=": if val=="" { return false }; return strings.Contains(actual,val)
